1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,493
The problem: quality guidelines are often prose, while releases
need repeatable decisions.

2
00:00:09,499 --> 00:00:15,298
Each case carries an input, an output and the reference or
context needed to judge it.

3
00:00:18,305 --> 00:00:24,053
JSON and YAML rubrics define criteria, weights and optional hard
thresholds.

4
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:33,463
Deterministic metrics check overlap, exact matches, numbers,
structure and other constraints.

5
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:42,499
An optional model judge uses a vendor-neutral chat interface for
custom criteria.

6
00:00:45,506 --> 00:00:52,467
The engine produces per-case breakdowns, JSON reports and an
interactive HTML dashboard.

7
00:00:55,474 --> 00:01:02,509
Token overlap is not semantic truth. A passing benchmark does
not prove broad reliability.

8
00:01:05,516 --> 00:01:12,193
The repository shows the scoring code, tests and benchmark.
Explore it from my portfolio.

